---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`What ${SITE.name} is, how it works, and why every tool runs entirely in your browser.`}
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <div class="container page">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        A small collection of developer utilities that run entirely in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Most developers keep a handful of browser tabs open for the same small jobs —
        formatting a JSON response, decoding a token, comparing two config files, checking
        what a timestamp means. This site is those jobs, collected in one place, built to
        be fast and to stay out of the way.
      </p>

      <h2>Everything runs in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        There is no backend. No server processes your input, because there is no server
        beyond the one that sent you this page. Every tool is JavaScript executing in your
        own tab, using the browser's built-in APIs — the Web Crypto API for hashing and
        signature verification, the native regular expression engine for pattern testing,
        <code>Intl</code> for date formatting.
      </p>
      <p>
        This matters practically, not just philosophically. It means you can paste a
        production JWT, an API response containing customer data, or an internal config
        file without that data leaving your machine. You do not have to take this on
        trust: open your browser's developer tools, switch to the Network tab, and use any
        tool on the site. You will see no outbound requests carrying your input.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static HTML generated by <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>. Each
        tool page ships one small interactive component and nothing else — no framework
        runtime on pages that do not need one, no analytics that follow you around, no
        cookie banner standing between you and a text box.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy and funding</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics that record page views and
        performance timings — not who you are or what you typed. It is funded by display
        advertising, kept to a small number of clearly-marked slots that never sit between
        you and a tool's controls. See the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>
        &nbsp;for the specifics.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections and requests</h2>
      <p>
        If a tool gives a wrong answer, that is a bug worth fixing — these are small,
        well-tested functions and they should be correct. If there is a utility you keep
        wishing were here, that is worth knowing too. New tools are added regularly.
      </p>

      <h2>Open source components</h2>
      <p>
        Almost everything here uses native browser APIs. Nineteen third-party libraries are
        included for the specific jobs the browser has no built-in for — every tool's own
        page also links the library it uses. All nineteen licences permit commercial use.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Library</th>
            <th scope="col">Licence</th>
            <th scope="col">Used in</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/kpdecker/jsdiff" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>diff</code></a></td><td>BSD-3-Clause</td><td>Diff Checker</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/blueimp/JavaScript-MD5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>blueimp-md5</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Hash Generator (text MD5, since the Web Crypto API deliberately omits it)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/satazor/js-spark-md5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>spark-md5</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Hash Generator (file MD5)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>qrcode-generator</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>QR Code Generator</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>js-yaml</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>JSON, YAML, CSV &amp; XML Converter (YAML)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/sql-formatter-org/sql-formatter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>sql-formatter</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>SQL Formatter</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/terser/terser" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>terser</code></a></td><td>BSD-2-Clause</td><td>HTML / CSS / JS Minifier (JavaScript)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dcodeIO/bcrypt.js" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>bcryptjs</code></a></td><td>BSD-3-Clause</td><td>Bcrypt Generator/Checker</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/svg/svgo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>svgo</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>SVG Optimizer</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/jamsinclair/jSquash/tree/main/packages/oxipng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>@jsquash/oxipng</code></a></td><td>Apache-2.0</td><td>Image Compressor (extra lossless PNG pass)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>fflate</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Image Compressor (zip download of a batch)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/ibezkrovnyi/image-quantization/tree/main/packages/image-q" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>image-q</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Image Compressor, Image Cropper, Image Format Converter (lossy PNG mode)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/spencermountain/compromise" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>compromise</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Word Counter (Sentence case proper-noun detection, loaded only on click)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/niieani/gpt-tokenizer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>gpt-tokenizer</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>LLM Token Counter (OpenAI's published token vocabularies)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/markedjs/marked" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>marked</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Markdown Previewer (Markdown → HTML)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>DOMPurify</code></a></td><td>MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0</td><td>Markdown Previewer (sanitizes the rendered HTML)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/mixmark-io/turndown" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>turndown</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Markdown Previewer (HTML → Markdown)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/domchristie/turndown-plugin-gfm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>turndown-plugin-gfm</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Markdown Previewer (GFM tables, strikethrough, task lists)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>onnxruntime-web</code></a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Background Remover, Face &amp; Plate Blur (on-device AI models via WebAssembly)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>AI models</h2>
      <p>
        Two tools also download a pre-trained model file — not an npm package like the
        libraries above, but a set of weights a neural network was trained on — to run
        entirely on-device via WebAssembly (<code>onnxruntime-web</code>, listed above). Both
        are freely licensed for commercial use, and both run exactly like every other tool
        here: nothing leaves your browser, ever, for the model to process.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Model</th>
            <th scope="col">Licence</th>
            <th scope="col">Used in</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">u2netp</a></td><td>Apache-2.0</td><td>Background Remover</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/onnx/models/tree/main/validated/vision/body_analysis/ultraface" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ultra-Light-Fast-Generic-Face-Detector-1MB</a></td><td>MIT</td><td>Face &amp; Plate Blur</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The site itself is open source (MIT licensed) — read the code powering any tool, or
        the privacy claims above, on <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
